 "readme": "State shots. 'target' is the 0-based index of the control in DOM order over all [data-ds-fixture-canvas] of the page, counting elements matching `button, [role=\"button\"], [role=\"radio\"], [role=\"switch\"], input:not([type=\"hidden\"]), textarea, select, [tabindex=\"0\"]` (deduped, natively disabled included). The viewer also renders state-matrix stories after the showcase stories; targets refer to the showcase stories only. Output: <page>.<name>.png cropped to the owning story canvas +/- 64 logical px, clipped to the viewport, and <page>.<name>.json {crop,story}. hover=pointer over; press=mouse down held; focus=Shift key then element.focus(); click=element.click(). 'native' (optional) is the control number on the native page when it differs (the viewer also counts tablists and tab panels, which are tab stops there). 'scroll' states: target is the story index, dx/dy scroll its first edge-fade scroller; 'clicks' repeats a click.",
